<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav ore output up slightly in Jan vs Dec.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav ore output up slightly in Jan vs Dec.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV NON-FERROUS ORES	JAN 97    DEC 96     JAN 96</p>
<p> copper ore (thousand tonnes)    1,467     1,436	1,632</p>
<p> lead-zinc ore			    58	  65	   59</p>
<p> bauxite				    --	  35	   15</p>
<p>NON-FERROUS METAL PRODUCTION</p>
<p> electrolytic copper (tonnes)    9,718    10,629	4,479</p>
<p> refined lead			  1,550	 930	2,568</p>
<p> zinc				    2,170     2,516	2,677</p>
<p> aluminium ingots		    5,419     4,208	1,741</p>
<p> refined silver (kilos)	    4,936     4,996     11,097</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 222 4305</p>
</text>
